  ],
  "after_setup_md": "## Monte Carlo VaR is a separate, asynchronous job\n\n`monte_carlo_var_parametric_normal` is not one of the functions below: Monte Carlo VaR runs as a\nqueued job. `POST /api/v1/var/compute` returns `202` with a `task_id`; poll\n`GET /api/v1/var/result/{task_id}` until `status` is `success`. The Python client does both for\nyou: `client.var.compute(portfolio_value=..., returns=[...], n_simulations=10000)` blocks and returns\nthe finished result. Simulation caps per tier are 10,000 (free), 100,000 (pro) and 500,000\n(enterprise); above your cap the call fails with `403`. The job counts against the same daily\nquota as every other call. Antithetic sampling is not exposed through the API.",
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "VaR and Expected Shortfall on a 10m portfolio",
      "intro": "Two years of daily log-returns in; the Basel one-day 99% VaR and the FRTB 97.5% Expected Shortfall out, as a fraction and in money. ES is the mean of the losses beyond the VaR threshold, so it is never smaller than VaR.",
      "calls": [
        {
          "function": "historical_simulation_var",
          "request": {
            "returns": "<returns:500>",
            "portfolio_value": 10000000,
            "confidence_level": 0.99
          },
          "returns": [
            "var_pct",
            "var_abs",
            "cvar_pct",
            "cvar_abs",
            "confidence_level",
            "n_obs"
          ]
        },
        {
          "function": "historical_expected_shortfall",
          "request": {
            "returns": "<returns:500>",
            "portfolio_value": 10000000,
            "confidence_level": 0.975
          },
          "returns": [
            "es_pct",
            "es_abs",
            "var_pct",
            "n_tail",
            "confidence_level"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Backtest result: capital multiplier and Kupiec test",
      "intro": "Six VaR breaches in 250 trading days. The first call gives the Basel traffic-light capital multiplier; the second tests whether 6 breaches is consistent with a 99% VaR model.",
      "calls": [
        {
          "function": "basel_capital_addon_multiplier",
          "request": {
            "n_breaches": 6
          },
          "returns": [
            "multiplier",
            "zone",
            "n_breaches"
          ]
        },
        {
          "function": "kupiec_pof_test",
          "request": {
            "n_breaches": 6,
            "n_observations": 250,
            "confidence_level": 0.99
          },
          "returns": [
            "lr_pof",
            "p_value",
            "critical_value",
            "reject"
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
